  "fieldNotes": {
    "truckGate": "Main truck drive off E Highland Rd (west curb cut) is a wide open multi-lane concrete drive with no barrier, gate, or booth (Street View 2021-09). A secondary east drive has a manual chain-link sliding gate with a Pepsi sign, but it is not the primary controlled entrance.",
    "entryLanes": "Main drive is a very wide unmarked concrete apron; no painted lane separation, so lane counts left null.",
    "dockDoors": "Dock banks on the NE (gray) building face (~12-14 trailers docked) plus the main building SE corner bank (~8-10) and east-face positions; band 25-50 is an overhead estimate.",
    "dropArea": "Dense trailer rows fill the east yard between the building and the pond, running from the rail corridor to E Highland Rd; 60+ drop positions plus a long nose-in row along the pond edge.",
    "multipleFacilities": "A dark-roof warehouse parcel at the SE corner sits inside the traced perimeter; Pepsi blue bottle shells are stacked around it (Street View), so it appears operationally Pepsi, but parcel ownership was not verified.",
    "shipRcvSeparate": "Two physically distinct dock clusters (NE gray-building bank vs main-building SE/east banks) suggest separate ship/receive; inferred from overhead only.",
    "railServed": "A rail corridor runs along the north boundary but no spur visibly enters the property."
